{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42796 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that p-Hydroxybenzoylcholine may interact with HepG2 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links p-Hydroxybenzoylcholine to VMRC-LCP, which is then targeted by Methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine, ultimately affecting HepG2. The second pathway connects p-Hydroxybenzoylcholine to Carboxylesterase 2, which targets a complex compound that also affects HepG2. The third pathway shows p-Hydroxybenzoylcholine targeting Raji, which is then targeted by Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, which also targets HepG2. These findings collectively suggest that p-Hydroxybenzoylcholine may exert its effects on HepG2 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving enzyme targets or signaling pathways. The mechanisms are not fully elucidated, but the shared target of HepG2 across multiple pathways indicates a potential role in cellular processes that are relevant to HepG2's function.",
